Most of those fantasy books were probably written since the sixties if I
am guessing right.  A LOT of old English and Irish folktales portray Elves
and Faries, Sprites, etc. as anything from mischevious and unpleasant to
downright Maelevolent.  Most modern fantasy novels seem to base their idea
of Elves on something similar to the Tolkien novels in which they are at
worst somewhat distant guardians of all that is beautiful and good.
Which is correct?  I guess by definition, in nethack Elves are chaotic and
those that don't like it are free to modify the source code.  

I'm not a big nethack guru, but I can't think of any way in which alignment
really makes that much difference other than what named weapons you can get.
Maybe if Elves were Lawful the combination of the ease in obtaining Excalibur
together with the number of intrinsics they start with would make the game
too easy?  On the other hand, being Chaotic means they get to rob shops with
impunity.  Six of one, half dozen of the other....

